From ca1bf85bb000385a5947aabead79422a6a2ef671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:38:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/28] (b) v2, part b-3: \@kernel@caption@unique for code that
 makes its own target

Round-4 finding R4-M3: the caption package (client path) needs the
unique name of a caption that other code leaves unstepped, but makes
its anchor itself in caption/prepare (with \@captiontargetfalse and
\hyper@makecurrent). It called the internal \@caption@uniqueH, saved and
restored \theH<type> itself, and relied on the kernel giving the number
reserved by \@caption@nostep@defs back before caption/prepare.

\@kernel@caption@unique{<counter>}{<code>} is now the documented
command for this: it executes <code> while \theH<counter> has the
suffix *<n> with the next <n> for that name (the same counting as the
kernel's own unique targets), and restores \theH<counter> afterwards
(also an undefined one). The contract is in ltfloat.dtx: every use
takes a new number; in the caption hooks and plugs no number is
reserved, so there are no gaps (the give-back is the kernel's business
now, not the client's). No group is added, so local assignments in
<code> survive (hyperref's \@currentHref with localanchorname).

The kernel's own \@caption@uniquetarget uses it as well, so it no longer
makes the target inside a group; the names are unchanged.

Test: caption-interface-003 (new): names in caption/prepare and in
caption/before counted with the kernel's targets, the number of a
\caption* before is given back, \theH restored, a counter without
\theH, local assignments kept.
